<title>USA: Weekend box office chart -- Jan 3-5.</title>
<headline>Weekend box office chart -- Jan 3-5.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the Jan. 3-5 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Michael		    $12,144,926	 $ 52,733,564</p>
<p>2. Jerry Maguire	    $12,030,145	 $ 83,006,355</p>
<p>3. Scream		     $10,015,810	 $ 39,084,452</p>
<p>4. 101 Dalmatians	   $ 7,342,467	 $121,788,625</p>
<p>5. One Fine Day	     $ 6,218,887	 $ 32,246,925</p>
<p>6. Beavis and Butt-head</p>
<p>    Do America		$ 5,755,741	 $ 54,149,743</p>
<p>7. Ghosts of Mississippi  $ 5,016,767	 $  5,782,753</p>
<p>8. The Preacher's Wife    $ 4,925,287	 $ 38,655,329</p>
<p>x. Mars Attacks!	    $ 3,433,575	 $ 33,779,762</p>
<p>x  My Fellow Americans    $ 3,330,333	 $ 18,004,594</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Michael&quot; was produced by now-defunct Turner Pictures, and released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc. &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.. &quot;101 Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;The Preacher's Wife&quot; are released by Disney. &quot;One Fine Day&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.. &quot;Beavis and Butt-head Do America&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Ghosts of Mississippi&quot; is produced by Castle Rock Entertainment, a unit of Time Warner, and released by Sony. &quot;Mars Attacks!&quot; and &quot;My Fellow Americans&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner.</p>
</text>
